Z||000000||rogergarrison||08-03-2001||04:10 PM||||I just had a thought as I passed another one on the road. Do people think there impressing the rest of us, or are we supposed to treat their vehicle special. Personally, I try to avoid running into anything, whether or not is full of show dogs. Maybe with the rash of busted Fieros here lately, we ought to have stickers on all our cars saying "CAUTION - SHOW CAR"<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||rockcrawl||08-03-2001||04:50 PM||||Yes, I always wondered about the horse trailers with a sign on the back that says "Caution Show Horses". Am I supposed to be more cautious than if it was just a car full of people or something. Whatever. Now a sign that says something like "Caution, Nitroglycerine" , well that's something to be extra cautious of.||||reg||7
